---
description: Coordinate the requested owned terminal work from actual session, checklist, check and retained-handoff evidence.
args:
  goal: string
returns: TerminalFindings
---
Determine the user's requested terminal state, observations, continuity exercise and any genuinely requested retained handoff. Compose the scoped terminal operator, checklist continuity assessment, installed-interface discovery and declared-check workflows according to actual evidence and dependencies. Pure action and outcome judgments compute values; only an admitted Native operation establishes an effect.

Keep the actual initial session and every performed operation's feedback. An opening grant permits an operation but does not request it. Preserve untouched checklist marks, other sessions and the retained workspace; honor explicit input method, viewport and ordering requirements. Distinguish a reattachment of the same running PTY from a restart or resume with a fresh PTY, and a genuine observed exit from merely losing a view.

Use the actual declared suite and complete result when the requested continuation depends on checks. A failed, truncated or unavailable prerequisite cannot authorize a dependent success. Discover installed interfaces or knowledge when it can resolve the request, rather than treating one discovery or check as an arbitrary global allowance. Do not repeat an unchanged refusal; use changed authoritative evidence to decide whether work can continue.

Return the requested supported findings as an answer, using actual final session/exit, check, discovery and retained-handoff evidence. The exact Native receipts remain operation evidence; do not add a generic receipt or status report. Keep a missing observation or refused effect explicit. Do not invent an event or receipt, claim that permission means completion, or replace a requested action with an explanation.
